<div class="interlude"><p>Some ideas only click once you see them move.</p></div>

<section id="how-it-works" class="section section--how">
  <div class="section__head">
    <h2 class="section__title">How it works</h2>
    <p class="section__lede">One idea, one short video. The goal is to make it click for someone else.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="how" data-controller="scene" data-scene-whoami-url-value="<%= Rails.configuration.x.hack_club_auth_whoami_url %>">
    <figure class="stage" aria-label="A small manim scene that follows the steps">
      <canvas data-scene-target="canvas"></canvas>
      <figcaption class="stage__caption" data-scene-target="caption"></figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step" data-scene-target="step">
        <span class="step__num c-yellow">1</span>
        <div class="step__body">
          <h3>Pick an idea.</h3>
          <p>Something you understand well enough to want to show someone: a proof, a pattern, a paradox, a trick from physics. If nothing comes to mind, borrow one from the examples below.</p>
          <code class="step__code">idea = <span class="c-teal">Text</span>(<span class="c-yellow">"<input class="code-input" value="why 0.999… = 1" maxlength="40" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Your idea" data-scene-target="idea" data-action="input->scene#retype focus->scene#showIdea">"</span>)</code>
          <p class="step__hint">Type your own idea.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step" data-scene-target="step">
        <span class="step__num c-blue">2</span>
        <div class="step__body">
          <h3>Animate it in manim.</h3>
          <p>The editor runs in your browser, so there’s nothing to install. Write a little Python, render it, watch, adjust, and render again. You can learn manim as you go.</p>
          <code class="step__code">self.<span class="c-teal">play</span>(<button type="button" class="code-token c-teal" data-scene-target="anim" data-action="scene#nextAnim" aria-label="Animation: Write. Click for another">Write</button>(idea), run_time=<button type="button" class="code-token code-drag c-purple" data-scene-target="runTime" data-action="pointerdown->scene#dragStart keydown->scene#nudge" aria-label="run_time in seconds; drag or use arrow keys">PI</button>)</code>
          <p class="step__hint">Click <em>Write</em> to swap the animation. Drag the number to change how long it runs.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step" data-scene-target="step">
        <span class="step__num c-green">3</span>
        <div class="step__body">
          <h3>Ship it.</h3>
          <p>Share the video and the code behind it. A real person watches it, and we mail you something back.</p>
          <code class="step__code">self.<span class="c-teal">ship</span>(video, repo)</code>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="examples" class="section" data-controller="sketch">
  <div class="section__head">
    <h2 class="section__title">Things worth animating</h2>
    <p class="section__lede">Each one is a question with a picture for an answer. Drag the yellow dot to play with it, or take one for your first scene.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cards">
    <%= render "pages/example", title: "Odd numbers make squares",
          body: "1 + 3 + 5 + 7 = 4². Each odd number is one more L wrapped around the square.",
          apis: "VGroup · LaggedStart · MathTex",
          play: "squares", hint: "Drag the corner to wrap another L." do %>
    <% end %>

    <%= render "pages/example", title: "Where sine comes from",
          body: "Spin a point around a circle and trace its height. That’s the whole wave.",
          apis: "TracedPath · always_redraw",
          play: "sine", hint: "Drag the point around the circle." do %>
      <line x1="20" y1="90" x2="306" y2="90" stroke="#3a3e45" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
    <% end %>

    <%= render "pages/example", title: "Euler’s identity",
          body: "Five constants, one line. Show why turning by π lands you on −1.",
          apis: "MathTex · Write · Rotate",
          play: "euler", hint: "Drag the point to −1." do %>
      <line x1="16" y1="96" x2="148" y2="96" stroke="#3a3e45" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
      <line x1="82" y1="30" x2="82" y2="162" stroke="#3a3e45" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
      <g data-d="o" font-family="Computer Modern Serif, Georgia, serif" font-style="italic" font-size="14" fill="#80868e">
        <text x="142" y="112" text-anchor="middle">1</text>
        <text x="22" y="112" text-anchor="middle">−1</text>
        <text x="90" y="36">i</text>
      </g>
    <% end %>

    <%= render "pages/example", title: "Pythagoras, rearranged",
          body: "Reshape the right triangle. However you pull it, the two smaller squares add up to the big one.",
          apis: "Transform · Rotate · Polygon",
          play: "pythagoras", hint: "Drag the top corner of the triangle." do %>
    <% end %>

    <%= render "pages/example", title: "Area under a curve",
          body: "Thinner and thinner rectangles, until they stop being rectangles and become the integral.",
          apis: "get_riemann_rectangles · ValueTracker",
          play: "riemann", hint: "Drag the dot to add rectangles." do %>
      <line x1="40" y1="150" x2="300" y2="150" stroke="#80868e" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
      <line x1="50" y1="24" x2="50" y2="156" stroke="#80868e" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
    <% end %>

    <%= render "pages/example", title: "Fourier epicycles",
          body: "Circles riding on circles can draw any shape. Even your name.",
          apis: "Circle · always_redraw · TracedPath",
          play: "fourier", hint: "Drag the dot to add circles." do %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="faq" class="section section--faq">
  <div class="section__head">
    <h2 class="section__title">Questions</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="faq">
    <details name="faq" open>
      <summary>What is manim?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <p>The Python library Grant Sanderson wrote to make the 3Blue1Brown videos. We use the free, open-source <a href="https://www.manim.community/">Manim Community</a> edition.</p>
    </details>
    <details name="faq">
      <summary>Who can join?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <p>Anyone 18 or under, anywhere in the world. It’s free.</p>
    </details>
    <details name="faq">
      <summary>I’ve never written Python. Can I still do this?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <p>Yes. A first scene is about ten lines: put a circle on screen, then make it do something. People in the Slack will help you debug.</p>
    </details>
    <details name="faq">
      <summary>What counts as math?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <p>Anything you can explain with a picture: proofs, patterns, probability, physics, algorithms, even the math hiding inside a game you like.</p>
    </details>
    <details name="faq">
      <summary>What do I get?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <p>Something real, in the mail, once you ship. You’ll pick it from a list, which we’ll share soon.</p>
    </details>
    <details name="faq">
      <summary>Where do I get help?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <p>Ask in the <a href="https://hackclub.com/slack/">Hack Club Slack</a>. Someone there has hit your error before.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

